{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"musophobic-repellent-ovenbird","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Mirror inventory finding F2 (reports/stability/mirror-inventory.md), MEDIUM.\n\n- src/rebar/signing.py:115 OPCERT_KINDS (exported in __all__ at :76) — canonical\n- src/rebar/opcert_service/jobs.py:38 VALID_KINDS (same 2)\n- src/rebar/_commands/remote_cert.py:24 _VALID_KINDS (same 2), plus a prose copy in _USAGE at :23\n\nNeither consumer imports the exported name; both gate client request validation. Churn is low\n(ADR 0049 fixes the count at two), but a miss silently rejects a legitimate kind.\n\nProposed fix: generate-from-canonical — import OPCERT_KINDS at both sites.","id":"6850-af5c-a4a1-4c5d","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Single-source the op-cert kinds across signing, opcert_service and remote_cert (mirror F2)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788317622517845001,"uuid":"c04b3f86-464f-4315-bd40-4536caabcbb1"}